  "method": "Playwright intercepts the browser's request for the named /ui/js/<file>.js and answers with the exact blob from git (git show <sha>:src/ui/<file>). It simulates a tab that already holds that module; it is NOT a real old tab. The PR changes only two UI modules (panel-fleet.js, accounts-view.js): every other module and shared asset is byte-identical at base and head, so there is no further retained-asset variation to test for this change.",
  "scope": "Throwaway fleet (isolated AGEND_HOME and HOME, own port, torn down afterwards), fake temporary named accounts 'work' (connected) and 'off' (not connected). The host's default account, ~/.claude and the :8452 preview were not touched. Real CLI sign-ins were not used. Agents were created in the throwaway fleet and read back from its fleet.yaml.",
  "disclosures": [
    "New panel-fleet.js with a retained accounts-view.js shows the RETAINED AccountSelect, so the create dialog's field carries the edit-dialog hint 'Changing the account restarts the agent...' (not the new create-specific copy). The choice still works: 'work' is written to the existing profile.",
    "With accounts-view.js@a2a77ad7d the field also uses the older 'sign in' words ('Fleet default (default sign-in)', 'off — not signed in').",
    "A retained create panel (panel-fleet.js@9458db49d) has no WSL Account field at all; creating without an account against the head server writes no backend_options, i.e. the default, exactly as before this PR."
  ],
  "checks_per_case": "dialog opens; WSL + Claude Code selectable; (field shown cases) named account 'work' is written as backend_options.claude-code.credential_profile=work and no new credential-profiles folder is made (only 'off' and 'work' exist); empty selection writes no credential_profile; desktop 1280x860 and phone 390x800; no page errors after sign-in.",
